---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Registration: Acuity appointment type "Calm Before Commands (Online Workshop)", Sun Sept 27 2026.
const ACUITY_APPOINTMENT_TYPE = '97862526';
const acuityUrl = `https://app.acuityscheduling.com/schedule.php?owner=24021188&appointmentType=${ACUITY_APPOINTMENT_TYPE}`;
---

<Layout
  title="Calm Before Commands: Free Online Dog Training Workshop | Down 4 Paws"
  description="Join CCDT dog trainer Pam Brown for a free 90-minute live online workshop on Sunday, September 27 at 11 AM ET. Learn why your dog seems to forget training when overwhelmed, and what to do before you repeat the cue."
>
  <!-- HEADER -->
  <header class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 bg-white shadow-sm">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 py-3.5 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="https://down4paws.com">
        <img src="/images/d4p-logo.png" alt="Down 4 Paws Dog Training" class="h-9 md:h-10" />
      </a>
      <a
        href="#register"
        class="font-display text-sm md:text-base bg-orange text-white px-5 py-2 rounded-full hover:bg-orange-bright transition-colors"
      >
        Save My Spot
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- 1. HERO -->
  <section class="bg-cream pt-24 md:pt-32 pb-12 md:pb-16">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 md:gap-8 items-center">
        <div class="md:col-span-7">
          <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-purple-mist text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full px-4 py-1.5 mb-6">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 bg-orange rounded-full"></span>
            Free live online workshop
          </p>

          <h1 class="font-display text-charcoal text-[clamp(1.9rem,4.6vw,3.2rem)] leading-[1.08] mb-5">
            Your dog knows it at home.
            <span class="text-orange block">Outside, it's like they never heard the word.</span>
          </h1>

          <p class="text-warm-gray text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-7">
            <strong class="text-charcoal font-semibold">Calm Before Commands</strong> is a free 90-minute workshop on why dogs seem to forget their training when they get overwhelmed, and what to do instead of repeating the cue louder.
          </p>

          <ul class="space-y-2 text-charcoal mb-8">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-1.5 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple flex-shrink-0"></span>
              <span><strong class="font-semibold">Sunday, September 27</strong> · 11:00 am to 12:30 pm Eastern</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-1.5 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple flex-shrink-0"></span>
              <span>Live online with Q&amp;A. Watch from your couch, dog optional.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-1.5 w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple flex-shrink-0"></span>
              <span>Free. Everyone who registers gets the replay.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <a
            href="#register"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 font-display bg-purple text-white text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-full hover:bg-purple-deep transition-colors"
          >
            Save My Free Spot
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
          </a>

          <p class="text-warm-gray text-sm mt-5">
            With <span class="text-charcoal font-semibold">Pam Brown, CCDT</span> · Down 4 Paws Dog Training, Norwood MA · 83 five-star Google reviews
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="md:col-span-5">
          <div class="relative rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl shadow-charcoal/10">
            <img
              src="/images/hero-split.jpg"
              alt="The same dog calm and relaxed at home on the left, then alert and braced on a busy path on the right"
              class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
              loading="eager"
            />
            <div class="absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 p-4">
              <span class="bg-white/90 backdrop-blur-sm text-charcoal font-display text-sm px-4 py-2 rounded-full shadow-sm">
                Calm at home. A different dog outside.
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. SOUND FAMILIAR + BEHAVIOR TRANSLATION -->
  <section class="bg-charcoal py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 md:gap-14">
        <div class="md:col-span-5">
          <p class="font-display text-orange text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-6">Sound familiar?</p>
          <ul class="space-y-6 text-white/90 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed font-light">
            <li>"He does a perfect sit in the kitchen. Another dog shows up and he acts like he's never heard the word."</li>
            <li>"She was doing so well. Then she hit adolescence and it feels like it all fell apart."</li>
            <li>"I said leave it four times. Louder each time. He stared right through me."</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="md:col-span-7">
          <p class="font-display text-orange text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-6">Here's the deal</p>
          <p class="font-display text-white text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-tight mb-8">
            Your dog probably isn't ignoring you.
          </p>

          <dl class="space-y-5 border-l-2 border-orange/60 pl-5">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-orange text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-1">What you see</dt>
              <dd class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed">A dog who "knows" the cue and won't do it.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-orange text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-1">What your dog may be feeling</dt>
              <dd class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed">Too much at once. New smells, movement, another dog. The brain is full.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-orange text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-1">Behavior Translation</dt>
              <dd class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed">Knowing a skill and being able to use it in the moment are two different things. An overwhelmed dog loses access to what they know.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-orange text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-1">Why it matters</dt>
              <dd class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed">Repeating the cue louder adds pressure to a dog who is already over capacity. The cue gets weaker, not stronger.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-orange text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-1">Next step</dt>
              <dd class="text-white/85 leading-relaxed">Notice earlier. Lower the difficulty. Help them recover. Then ask.</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>

          <p class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-white/10 font-display text-white text-xl md:text-2xl">
            Your dog isn't giving you a hard time.<br />
            <span class="text-orange">They're having a hard time.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. WHAT YOU'LL WALK AWAY WITH -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
        <p class="font-display text-orange text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">In 90 minutes</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-charcoal text-3xl md:text-4xl leading-tight mb-4">
          What you'll walk away with
        </h2>
        <p class="text-warm-gray text-lg leading-relaxed">
          One idea, taught properly. Not forty tips you'll forget by Tuesday.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        <div class="bg-cream rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-7 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-display text-purple text-lg mb-2">The early signs of overstimulation</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed">Staring, scanning, pulling harder, grabbing treats roughly, slower responses. So you catch it before the bark, the lunge, or the shutdown.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-cream rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-7 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-display text-purple text-lg mb-2">Notice → Process → Reconnect → Respond</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed">The four-step framework for what to do before you give another command. When to pause, when to add distance, when movement helps.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-cream rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-7 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-display text-purple text-lg mb-2">Why "she regressed" is normal</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed">What adolescence does to a dog who was doing great, and what actually helps. Bad days don't erase progress.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-cream rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-7 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-display text-purple text-lg mb-2">Five things to try this week</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray leading-relaxed">Real walks, real visitors, real life. No perfect conditions required.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a
          href="#register"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 font-display bg-purple text-white text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-full hover:bg-purple-deep transition-colors"
        >
          Save My Free Spot
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. PROOF + PAM -->
  <section class="bg-cream py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <p class="font-display text-orange text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-8">Real dogs, real life</p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 mb-14">
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-semibold text-charcoal mb-1">Archie</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-warm-gray mb-4">Mixed breed, young adult</p>
          <p class="text-charcoal/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Great in training sessions. Neighborhood walks were a different story: pulling, reacting to dogs on porches, overstimulated before the walk even started. The fix wasn't more commands. It was getting his attention earlier, creating space sooner, and keeping him in walks he could actually handle.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-beige">
          <p class="font-semibold text-charcoal mb-1">Maisie</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-warm-gray mb-4">Golden Retriever, puppy</p>
          <p class="text-charcoal/80 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Good at home. Outside with stimulation, she fell apart. After a day of walk, car ride, errands and meeting a new dog, she couldn't settle at all that night. Once her owner learned to spot the overload and build in rest, the evenings calmed down.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-purple rounded-2xl p-6 text-white">
          <p class="text-white/70 text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Google review</p>
          <p class="text-white/95 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            "Before Pam, whenever he saw another dog on a walk, he would start barking and lunging. After Pam, he clocks another dog but does not get distracted or reactive."
          </p>
          <p class="text-white/70 text-xs">Arthur's family</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center bg-white rounded-3xl p-7 md:p-10 border border-beige">
        <div class="md:col-span-3 flex justify-center md:justify-start">
          <img src="/images/pam-profile.jpg" alt="Pam Brown, CCDT, Down 4 Paws Dog Training" class="w-32 h-32 md:w-40 md:h-40 rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-md" />
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-9">
          <p class="font-display text-purple text-xl mb-1">Pam Brown, CCDT</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray text-sm mb-4">Founder &amp; Head Trainer, Down 4 Paws Dog Training</p>
          <p class="text-warm-gray text-lg leading-relaxed">
            I train force-free, in real neighborhoods, with real families in the Boston suburbs. Almost every family I meet says the same thing first: "He knows this. He's just not listening." This workshop is the other way to look at it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. REGISTER -->
  <section id="register" class="bg-charcoal py-16 md:py-24 scroll-mt-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
      <div class="text-center mb-8">
        <p class="font-display text-orange text-sm tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">Free registration</p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-white text-3xl md:text-4xl mb-3">Save your spot</h2>
        <p class="text-white/80 text-lg">Sunday, September 27 · 11:00 am to 12:30 pm ET · Live online</p>
        <p class="text-white/50 text-sm mt-2">Can't make it live? Register anyway. Everyone who registers gets the replay.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Acuity Embed: Calm Before Commands, Sept 27, 2026 -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-3xl shadow-2xl shadow-black/20 overflow-hidden">
        <iframe
          src={acuityUrl}
          width="100%"
          height="800"
          frameborder="0"
          allow="payment"
          title="Workshop Registration"
          class="block w-full min-h-[500px]"
        ></iframe>
      </div>
      <script is:inline src="https://embed.acuityscheduling.com/js/embed.js"></script>

      <div class="mt-12 space-y-3">
        <details class="group bg-white/5 rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-white font-semibold list-none flex justify-between items-center">
            Do I need my dog with me?
            <span class="text-orange group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-white/75 mt-3 leading-relaxed">No. This one is for you. Watch, take notes, then practice this week.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white/5 rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-white font-semibold list-none flex justify-between items-center">
            Is it only for reactive dogs?
            <span class="text-orange group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-white/75 mt-3 leading-relaxed">No. It's for any dog who does great at home and struggles outside, in adolescence, around visitors, or in busy places.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white/5 rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-white font-semibold list-none flex justify-between items-center">
            Is this a sales pitch?
            <span class="text-orange group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-white/75 mt-3 leading-relaxed">The workshop stands on its own. At the end I'll tell you how to work with me if you want more support, including a new virtual option. That's it.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white/5 rounded-xl px-5 py-4">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-white font-semibold list-none flex justify-between items-center">
            Do I need to be near Boston?
            <span class="text-orange group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-white/75 mt-3 leading-relaxed">No. It's online. Join from anywhere.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <footer class="bg-white border-t border-beige py-10">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <img src="/images/d4p-logo.png" alt="Down 4 Paws" class="h-9" />
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-warm-gray">
        <a href="https://down4paws.com" class="hover:text-purple transition-colors">down4paws.com</a>
        <span class="w-1 h-1 bg-warm-gray/30 rounded-full"></span>
        <a href="https://instagram.com/down4paws" class="hover:text-purple transition-colors">@down4paws</a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-warm-gray/50">&copy; 2026 Down 4 Paws</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style is:global>
    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
    details summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  </style>
</Layout>
